From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: snd-xenon: port to 6.18, enable HDMI audio, drop the unused IRQ

Free60's Xbox 360 sound driver (2009) for 6.18:
- from_timer -> timer_container_of, del_timer_sync -> timer_delete_sync,
  pci_{alloc,free}_consistent -> dma_{alloc,free}_coherent (outside the
  spinlock; keep the DMA handle for freeing, the device takes it masked),
  snd_printk -> dev_err/dev_warn.
- Reset the DAC through the SMC GPIOs and turn HDMI audio on over the
  SMC's I2C (module parameter hdmi, default on), as libxenon's
  xenon_sound_init does. Without it the DMA pointer never moved.
- Don't request the interrupt: the driver polls on a timer and never
  acknowledged it, which made an interrupt storm.

Built as a module with CONFIG_SOUND=m, CONFIG_SND=m, CONFIG_SND_PCI=y,
CONFIG_SND_XENON=m (no change to the kernel image). Playback runs at
48 kHz (hw_ptr advances ~48000 frames/s); output on the TV not yet heard.

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
